  <text>
    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="80">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:IICn">II Cn</ref> 80</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ic wylle, þ<hi rend="italic">æt</hi> ælc man si his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda ⁊ on felda on his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-a">And ic wille, þæt ælc man sy his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda ⁊ on fealda on his aganan.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="80" corresp="#wit-q">Uolo, ut omnis homo sit uenatione sua dignus in nemore et in campo in dominio suo.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#robertson" n="80" corresp="#wit-b">Be huntnaðe. And ic wylle þæt ælc man sy his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda ⁊ on felda on his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And ic wylle þæt ælc man si his huntnoðes wyrðe on wuda and on felda on his agenan.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-b">Concerning hunting. And it is my will that every man shall be entitled to hunt in the woods and fields on his own property.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-g-a">And it is my desire that each person be entitled to hunt in his own woods and fields.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#whitelock">And it is my will that every man is to be entitled to his hunting in wood and field on his own land.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann">(Von Jagd. B) Und ich will, das jedermann seiner Jagd theilhaftig sei in Wald und Feld auf seinem Eigen.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">(Of hunting. B) And I will that every man be entitled to his hunting in wood and field on his own land.</ab>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_4-2">CHn cor 4.2</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_5">CHn cor 5</ref></note>
        <note type="comparedBy" source="#wormald-mel" n="401"><ref target="clause:CHnCor_6">CHn cor 6</ref></note>
